Looks fierce, with fire in her eyes,
Hair undone—no need for disguise.
Hands unbound, heart untamed,
She doesn’t hold back, won’t play the game.

She’s a fighter, fragile in disguise,
Won’t blink at injustice, won’t swallow lies.
Loud and right, she claims her space,
Curses the silence, dares the race.

She’ll bend the rules, break the mold,
To get her truth heard, fierce and bold.
She is free—wild wind, not a breeze,
Won’t sit back, won’t beg or please.

She doesn’t care what they think of me...
Because she is not me
